or on our website. Valerie Hathorn managed a Dairy Queen fast food restaurant in the small city of Mount Vernon, Ohio. One of her employees was 32-year-old Tina Herman, a good friend and one of the most reliable people Valerie knew. Tina loved her job and her colleagues and she had never missed a shift or abandoned her responsibilities. So when she failed to show up for work on the afternoon of Wednesday, November 10, 2010, Valerie noticed. immediately. She tried calling Tina, but there was no answer. Growing uneasy, Valerie drove to the house that Tina shared with her boyfriend Greg Borders and her two children from a previous relationship, 13-year-old Sarah and 11-year-old Cody Maynard. Although Tina worked in Mount Vernon, she lived about

