nine miles outside town in the planned community of Apple Valley. Something of a resort area, Apple Valley surrounds a 511-acre reservoir named Apple Valley Lake. With rolling hills, tree-dotted landscapes and lakefront homes, it seemed like an idyllic place to raise a family. Tina's house sat on a somewhat isolated stretch of a street called King Beach Drive with a large wooded area across the road. When Valerie arrived, the inside lights were on and Tina's blue, 2000 Ford pickup truck was parked in the driveway, but no one answered the door. She left a note before leaving. Later that evening, still having heard nothing from Tina, Valerie called the county sheriff's office to request a welfare check. A deputy arrived at Tina's house at around 8 p.m.,

